# Vulnerability ignore list for the gateway image and its runtime requirements. Read by
# Trivy (gateway image scans in ci.yml and release.yml) and by pip-audit (CI passes every
# non-comment line as --ignore-vuln). Every entry: the affected component, why it cannot be
# fixed here and why it does not apply, and when it is re-evaluated. Drop an entry as soon
# as an upstream release carries the fix.

# 2026-10-29 (#117): ten more filelock 3.x advisories, fixed in 4.0.9/4.2.1; still blocked by
# LiteLLM's filelock<4.0 cap. All are local (AV:L, PR:L): they need a second local user who can
# write near the lock path or swap a symlink/inode under it (UnixFileLock, StrictSoftFileLock,
# SoftFileLock, SoftReadWriteLock, ReadWriteLock), or are Windows-only (WindowsFileLock). The
# gateway pod is one non-root user on a read-only root filesystem. Re-evaluate on every
# Dependabot bump of litellm; remove with the #88 entries once it allows filelock 4.2.1.
CVE-2026-112908
CVE-2026-112909
CVE-2026-112910
CVE-2026-112911
CVE-2026-112912
CVE-2026-112915
CVE-2026-112935
CVE-2026-112936
CVE-2026-112938
CVE-2026-112939

# 2026-10-27 (#88): filelock 3.x, fixed in 4.2.1. LiteLLM up to 1.106.4 requires
# filelock<4.0, so no pin resolves. GHSA-v4x8-3wr5-3wq8 is in ReadWriteLock, which LiteLLM
# never uses, and needs a second local user; the gateway pod is one non-root user on a
# read-only root filesystem. The other two are Windows-only. Re-evaluate on every
# Dependabot bump of litellm; remove once it allows filelock 4.2.1.
CVE-2026-112940
GHSA-v4x8-3wr5-3wq8
CVE-2026-112913
GHSA-9vhv-jxww-xfm5
CVE-2026-112907
GHSA-567q-5qvw-pf92
